  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given that the inverse trigonometric functions take principal values only. Then, the number of real values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;which satisfy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi></math> is equal to:</p>"
  },
